@startuml restart-survival
!pragma layout smetana
!include ../_includes/theme.puml

title Surviving a host restart: today and target

left to right direction

rectangle "Today: pty backend" {
  node "tb-sessiond" as D1 $SERVICE {
    component "Claude PTY master" as P1 $AGENT
  }
  node "Codex app-server\n(separate process)" as A1 $AGENT
  D1 --> A1 : app-server socket
  note bottom of D1
    A host restart closes the PTY master:
    Claude sessions end and resume later
    by --resume UUID.
    Codex is re-adopted through thread/resume.
  end note
}

rectangle "Target (historical, superseded by Arch v1 §A7 + PR #8)" {
  node "Session host" as D2 $SERVICE
  node "Per-session terminal holders\n(pty holder process or ax;\ntmux superseded 2026-10-05)" as T2 $SERVICE {
    component "Claude PTY" as P2 $AGENT
    component "Codex" as C2 $AGENT
  }
  D2 --> T2 : create, attach,\ninject, observe
  note bottom of T2
    Historical no-hangup target.
    Requested restarts use park-and-restart
    with confirmed stops (Arch v1 §A7, PR #8).
    People attach through the holder
    (control or read-only).
  end note
}

D1 -[hidden]-> D2

caption Sources: docs/claude-goal-runtime.md "The daemon owns the PTY master"; docs/codex-goal-runtime.md; agent-session-manager-spec §1.3, §3, §4; spec §5, §13, §14 (target: historical, superseded; see §14)
@enduml
